# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Bustfile — fail-closed stop conditions for Hermeneia
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: bust.ncl
# The probes below exercise synthetic repository-local tests; they do not inject
# faults into a user's data, mutate tracked files, or contact external systems.

@abstract:
Bust defines conditions under which Hermeneia must stop rather than report a
successful or licensed answer. Current stop conditions are grounded in the
implemented `.hil` parser, JSONL loader, IR validator, and external checker
seam. Failure of the checker, malformed input, or an unimplemented voke must
never be converted to `p-sufficient` or an empty successful result.

Hermeneia currently has no runtime certificate, token, or grant whose expiry
can be checked. No expiry condition is invented here. Any new remote service,
credential, or destructive failure drill requires owner review and a bounded,
repository-local test plan first.
@end

## Failure Modes

### unsupported-voke-must-stop
- class: unsupported_operation
- description: A recognized but unimplemented voke must return an explicit not-implemented error rather than successful empty output
- injection_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-syntax other_vokes_are_unimplemented_not_syntax_errors
- recovery_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-core plans_the_readme_example
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 30
- status: declared
- notes: The injection is a synthetic parser fixture; the recovery probe checks the supported invoke planning path.

### missing-checker-must-not-pass
- class: oracle_unavailable
- description: Missing tropecheck or checker I/O failure must not be interpreted as a passing verdict
- injection_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-cli --features e2e --test slice missing_checker_exits_three_with_instructions
- recovery_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-cli --test gate the_slice_workflow_supplies_a_checker
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 60
- status: declared
- notes: The named test removes PATH and HERMENEIA_TROPECHECK only inside its child process; CI must still supply a real checker for the full slice.

### malformed-store-data-must-stop
- class: malformed_input
- description: Malformed JSONL and deceptive grades must be rejected before planning or verdict rendering
- injection_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-store malformed_line_reports_its_number
- recovery_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-store seed_corpus_loads
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 30
- status: declared
- notes: The test uses an in-memory synthetic line and does not alter the checked-in corpus.

### loss-or-warrant-must-not-be-fabricated
- class: false_license
- description: A requested loss vector or warrant must be refused when the current checker/store interface cannot provide it
- injection_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-core show_loss_is_refused_honestly
- recovery_probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-core plans_the_readme_example
- expected_recovery_time_seconds: 30
- status: declared
- notes: This protects the documented evidence boundary: unsupported output is an error, not an invented explanation.
